    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_f81c7aad",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: mysogynous; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes two images: the top image shows a woman (from 'The Hunger Games') aiming a bow and arrow, labeled 'what women think they'll do when the economy collapses,' implying preparedness and self-reliance. The bottom image shows a woman in a revealing outfit leaning into a car window to flirt with a man, labeled 'vs what they'll actually do,' implying that women will resort to prostitution or transactional relationships in economic hardship. This is a misogynistic stereotype that devalues women's competence and portrays them as morally or practically inferior in crisis situations, reinforcing harmful gender norms and objectifying women by reducing their potential actions to sexualized behavior. The meme uses a false dichotomy to mock women's perceived lack of practical survival skills and instead frames their response to economic collapse as morally questionable or sexually motivated, which is a form of mysogynous content.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_a54c5fe1"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
